OL,3,GNEWSAStory behind the shipwreck
OL,4,Arevealed at low tide
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt first glance, it resembles a rocky
OL,7,Foutcrop beneath chalk cliffs, but a
OL,8,Fcloser look reveals a shipwreck.
OL,10,FThe SS Rosa sank off Flamborough, East
OL,11,FYorkshire, in 1930 and the remains,
OL,12,Fincluding a large boiler rising above
OL,13,Fthe seabed, were captured on camera at
OL,14,Flow tide last week.
OL,16,FSo how did ship meet its fate? Dr Robb
OL,17,FRobinson, a maritime historian, has
OL,18,Fbeen tracing its story.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,384,380,200,160,0,100
